# The party's banter halfway down the Passenger Car, before the Phantom strikes at its far end (Ashwin, 2026-11-02: explore
# the car first, a little banter, then the fight at the other side). Region ghostlight_express.
# Started by: the windows prop on ghostlight_g1_passenger (`call`, `approach: 3`, after the Vagrant's welcome and before the
# Phantom's fight). Written in-thread, not drafted by Gemini (the bridge wasn't reachable); redraft through it if wanted.

~ start
Narrator: Halfway down the aisle the lamps burn steady, and for a moment the car is only a car: warm brass, red velvet and the clack of wheels under your boots.
interject name:silas_vane: Every bench taken and not one soul willing to cut the deck. Worst crowd I ever sat down with.
interject name:delphine_ravelle: Hush, darling, they're an audience. They're simply waiting for the second act.
interject name:tobin_hayward: Back home we sat up with the dead the night before a burying. Nobody said they'd be riding along after.
interject name:rook_coldwake: Floor's level and she holds the rail through the bends. Whoever laid this line knew the trade, ties or no ties.
interject name:lucan_houndstooth: Then tell me why the air goes sour toward the front. Tallow back here, and up ahead something gone over, like meat left in the sun.
interject name:cordelia_skein: Rot in a carriage of the bodiless. Now that is a contradiction worth a closer look.
interject class:fighter: Keep close going forward. If something's wrong up there, we meet it together.
Narrator: Near the far end of the car, a tall figure waits in the aisle, perfectly still, its head tilted a little too far to one side.
